# S4, critic and closure of the shader bank (12 October 2026)

The bank now holds 86 blocks, all green on the full verifier in both directions, with a stricter criterion than before; ten blocks were added to cover the onekey-pro-2 looks, every look has a written composition, and the arch glow look composed from the bank lowers the fitting error on the three proof frames from 41.3, 39.4 and 39.7 to 32.5, 28.7 and 25.8 (RMS in 8-bit levels), while remaining far from a faithful match, for reasons measured below. No block failed, so nothing was quarantined and no file was deleted. (12 October 2026)

## 1. Verifier on the whole bank, and what was fixed (12 October 2026)

The first run on the 76 blocks inherited from S0, S2 and S3 was green (exit 0, 27.5 s). That verdict, however, rested on the mean error alone, and S2 had already shown that a geometric error confined to a small area passes under it (`sdf_arc` widened by 30 degrees: mean 1.76, max 255). The verifier therefore received a second criterion, set in `settings.json` (`shaders.verify_outlier_levels` 8, `shaders.verify_outlier_share_max` 0.001): a case is red when more than 0.1 % of its pixels differ by more than 8 levels in their worst channel. The previous verifier is kept at `/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-motion-design/docs/build/S4-critic/VerifyShaderBank.before-S4.py`. (12 October 2026)

The stricter verifier, run as a stress test (4 random sets, 320 px, seed 777), turned three S3 blocks red, each for a float32 against float64 disagreement at a floor:

| Block | Symptom | Cause | Fix in `Scripts/HarvestNoisePost.py` |
|---|---|---|---|
| `dither_bayer_ramp` | 0.15 % outliers, steps of 76.75 levels | exact rational ties: at 320 px, `3j + 5 idx + 4 = 320 n` has integer solutions, so `t (L - 1) + th` lands exactly on a level | odd offset `QUANT_EPS = 0.000613` inside the floor, in both languages |
| `dither_ign_ramp` | 0.17 % outliers | the IGN fract chain drifts by about 1e-4 between float32 and float64 at large cell indices | same offset, and the twin computes the IGN threshold in float32 |
| `grain_film` | 0.18 % outliers at 513 px | one row of cells floors differently | the twin rebuilds the fragment uv in float32 exactly as the shader does (`x / res`, `1 - y / res`) |

After the fixes, the three blocks are green at 256, 320, 384, 513, 720 and 1000 px. One residual remains: `grain_film` at 1000 px, seed 5, shows exactly one flipped row (share 0.00100, equal to the limit, so green); the GPU probably fuses a multiply-add there, which numpy cannot imitate. The previous folders are kept at `/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-motion-design/docs/build/S4-critic/dither-before/`. Every other twin is unchanged: the SHA-256 of all 39 S3 twins was compared before and after the regeneration of their metadata. (12 October 2026)

