## 5. Arch glow wallpaper on the device screen: composition and fitting proof (12 October 2026)

**Diagnosis of the old fit.** `zrmd/shaders/archglow.py` ramps its colours on the vertical distance `v - va(x)`. On a steep flank that distance grows much faster than the true distance, so the bright band thins out along the flanks and the fit had to flatten the arch into a chevron to keep any band at all (visible on `/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-motion-design/motions/onekey-d01-device-pullback/V_008/archglow-board.png`). The bank block `arch_glow_field` keeps the same layers but ramps on the first-order normal distance in canvas heights, `(v - va) / sqrt(1 + slope^2)` with the slope corrected by the screen aspect, and lets the side drift follow the height (`side_axis`), since the amber lies low on the flanks. (12 October 2026)

**Composition** (`compose.py` layers, bottom first):

```json
[{"block": "arch_glow_field", "params": {"aspect": 0.632, "...": "fitted"}},
 {"block": "solid_color", "params": {"color": "droplet"}, "mask": {"block": "sdf_circle", "params": {"center": ["cx", "dot_y"], "radius": "dot_r", "soft": 0.003, "aspect": 0.632}}},
 {"block": "glow_ring", "blend": "add", "params": {"color": "ring", "center": ["cx", "dot_y"], "radius": "dot_r", "sigma": "fitted", "intensity": "fitted", "aspect": 0.632}}]
```

**Method.** `/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-motion-design/ZenRayMotionDesign/Scripts/FitArchGlowBank.py` reuses the crop function of `Scripts/FitArchGlow.py` (V_008 device track, grey opening, 64 x 100 screen crop), fits 42 parameters on the numpy twins by least squares from 18 starts (apex, k, p) on 16 processes, refines the best, then renders the same layer list as GLSL at 64 x 100 and 640 x 1000. Total 74 s. (12 October 2026)

| Frame | Time | Old `archglow.py` RMS | Bank, iteration 1 (normal distance) | Bank, iteration 2 (plus `side_axis`) | GLSL against crop | GLSL against numpy, mean / max |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 10 | 1.500 s | 41.28 | 35.24 | 32.46 | 32.46 | 0.23 / 0.5 |
| 48 | 2.133 s | 39.41 | 30.30 | 28.70 | 28.70 | 0.11 / 0.5 |
| 92 | 2.866 s | 39.73 | 26.67 | 25.81 | 25.82 | 0.16 / 0.5 |

The GLSL render reproduces the fitted numpy evaluation to a fraction of a level, so the improvement is real on the GPU path, and the 640 x 1000 renders are sharp (`/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-motion-design/docs/build/S4-critic/fit/frame048-glsl-640x1000.png`). Board, crop against GLSL against HD: `/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-motion-design/docs/build/S4-critic/fit/board-crop-glsl-hd.png`; parameters and layers: `fit/fit-arch-glow-bank.json`; iteration 1 in `fit-iter1/`. The crops in those folders are analysis data only. (12 October 2026)

**Why the error is still about 26 to 32 levels, read from the fitted values and the board.** Several parameters end on their bounds (`w_out` at its minimum 0.02, `side` at [0.5, 1.0]), and the fitter darkens `c_core_side` almost to black: it uses the side drift to imitate a falloff the model lacks, which says the structure, not the optimiser, is the limit. Three causes stand out. First, the reference has a broad warm region filling the lower flanks outside the arch, whereas the model only has a warm rim; a second `arch_glow_field` (or `gradient_stops6` along the height) in `screen` blend, masked to the lower flanks, should carry it. Second, the thin cyan line and deep blue rim on the arch edge are narrower than one crop pixel at 64 x 100, so the fit should move to a crop of at least 192 x 298 (the device's `screen_px`). Third, frame 10's crop contains the device frame and its blue reflection around a rounded screen, not the wallpaper alone, which no wallpaper model can fit; the screen should be masked by a `sdf_rounded_rect` and the RMS measured inside it. The droplet also fell into a grey disc on frame 92, a local minimum that a fixed dark colour would avoid. These are the next steps, in this order, and each is a parameter or a layer, never a texture. (12 October 2026)

